s the fastest way to ensure we don't have issues. We can fix it later."],["5f5907fd_9307f38b",85,-1,1,"disabled"],["da865f7e_bca5485e",68,-1,1,"Not needed."],["e305968b_7747617f",68,-1,0,"Optional nit: If you have the interface class include a pure virtual weakptr getter, then we can avoid having to plumb weakptrs in a bunch of function signatures and instead get the weakptr when we…"],["fb7c7e42_76ff1a49",86,-1,1,"Should this live in the mock class?"]],0,102],[7151158,20406,560,14.011,11.533,[[0,0.981,58,551],[5,0.019,22,9]],[["1bf9bcaa_4f32736e",67,-1,1,"To be \"accurate\" this should happen after AttemptLogin is called."],["433545d4_6b3ebdc1",68,-1,1,"I wouldn't do this here. It lets everyone now refer to the proto as ActorLoginCredentialFiller::AttemptLoginDetail and it's not actually a type specific to the filler, but a convenience."],["88705d6f_7d329c08",67,-1,0,"Thank you!"],["c31d8701_83c01c58",67,-1,1,"This should come right before reset if you want to test that the `reset` is responsible for calling the logger."],["d7d83be2_a6963dcf",72,-1,1,"Optional: Remove \"Outcome\" from all enum values."],["d9ae4d4c_f3d05865",68,-1,1,"There is probably a better map here:https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:base/containers/README.md"],["e10e2e37_3c96087c",69,-1,1,"Eventually we actually need a form identifier that we can fetch the form data for. For now though,anything that allows us to pair the username and password fields restuls is good enough."],["e5538241_b83388a2",69,-1,1,"I think we should separate the biometric auth out of this."],["e618ce1d_a1035fe6",68,-1,1,"This is not unique per page. Only per frame. Eventually we actually need a form identifier that we can fetch the form data for or we somehow bundle the pre-parsed form data. For now though,anything…"],["72aa13a5_3ab8adb6",69,0,1,"+reauth_duration?"],["aa69af85_80d558f3",69,0,1,"Let's use kUnknown for now and add a TODO to then add kFillingNotAllowed to the proto and change it. kDisallowedOrigin means somthing else."],["c44c0792_7dbe3dbf",69,0,1,"Same here: +?"],["c8defeb0_e59e0d91",69,0,1,"Only set this in ReauthenticateAndFill."],["f2ded44a_8701664d",69,0,1,"nit: [form_id, filling_result], so that you don't need to use pair.second, which isn't very descriptive."]],0,103],[7157373,20406,73,3.042,2.433,[[5,0.595,23,44],[18,0.266,4,20],[0,0.139,59,9]],[],0,104],[7157888,20406,42,1.77,1.388,[[18,5]],[],0,105],[7184579,20413,381,11.412,9.682,[[0,0.936,60,358],[7,0.041,22,13],[10,0.023,10,8]],[["06839c74_6e8db40a",53,0,1,"This means permission for app and site will appear identical to the user. Why not deduplicate already and only show a single permission for a credential?"],["1880845a_4563d954",39,0,1,"Would you mind adding a TODO here for changing this to a `url.mojom.Url`?"],["47c7b0f5_14f3ab3c",87,0,1,"nit: surround by backticks"],["49dee3d2_abcba8c5",87,0,1,"https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/main/styleguide/c++/c++-features.md#default-comparisons-allowed You should also default ==. In addittion, the recommendation is to use non-member…"],["4dd6f81f_d98b4664",39,0,0,"Nit for a future CL: it would be ideal if this was a `url.mojom.URL`, not a string."],["528b8442_23857193",53,0,1,"Don't use auto unless the exact type is readable from this line of code or the once in the immediate vicinity. It harms code readability and has no advantage."],["5c06176a_f1d4d648",39,0,0,"In //chrome/browser/ui/webui/password_manager/password_manager_ui_handler.cc, you populate this with an empty `DomainInfo` if the flag is disabled. Did you consider making it optional instead?…"],["5e224ad0_d92aa05f",39,0,0,"This would ideally be a `url.mojom.URL`."],["8d08e3fe_28fcb4b3",53,0,1,"Can this happen? I think not. If not, let's add a CHECK with NotFatalUntil M144/145"],["8fbdd8a0_0f3743b0",39,0,1,"Won't it be cleaner and less changes if you just introduce signon_realm into ActorLoginPermission? You'll populate and use it only if a feature is enabled."],["9a734b9c_dddfc68b",53,0,0,"I know this is not very common although there might be multiple credentials with the same signon_realm and username but different password."],["9aa94ea4_bdeecf12",53,0,1,"Please process forms differently depending on the feature flag so that you can move out `affiliated_domains` out of the forms loop. It should also make code easier to follow."],["f99be235_bafcae47",53,0,0,"This looks like a bug. When we compare forms we compare signon_realms. Is this consistent with how permissions are stored?"]],0,106],[7207404,20419,27,1.081,0.837,[[0,61]],[],0,107],[7207334,20420,118,4.374,3.405,[[0,0.718,62,87],[7,0.153,23,17],[10,0.092,11,10],[12,0.038,11,4]],[],0,108],[7201454,20420,206,6.218,5.034,[[0,0.887,63,187],[7,0.059,24,10],[10,0.027,12,5],[8,0.014,6,2],[12,0.014,12,2]],[["0f4dfc7d_6cab052f",60,-2,1,"What if you make it explicit and update API to accept `signon_realm` and `username` to revoke the permission?"],["604fb699_77da9474",2,-2,1,"This really sounds like 2 CLs in one. Please split clean-ups from code changes for ease of review."],["b9e2c8be_44f3d641",53,-2,0,"Not needed?"],["14649c53_e1ce3509",39,-1,1,"I won't insist on it, but I agree with Ioana that this would have been easier to review if you had split these two unrelated changes into distinct CLs."],["4afe4bce_36c50bdf",88,-1,1,"Can we remove this? So that nobody accidentally uses it without understanding the consequences."],["4bc8dee4_f4c76fcd",88,-1,1,"Nit: You can forward-declare this in the `.h` file."]],0,109],[7075293,20420,4,0.538,0.375,[[0,0.778,64,3],[7,0.222,25,1]],[],0,110],[7255975,20438,51,1.77,1.388,[[7,26]],[["2099b89c_1855d935",89,-1,1,"It's a very indirect check with a comment reminding a logical riddle. Can you simply check the state of the controller that there is no dialog?"]],0,111]]}